    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Persistent energy market volatility is fueling a surge in trading activity on EEX as utilities, producers, and traders actively hedge power and gas price risk. This lifted full-year activity and produced double-digit volume growth in early 2026. Beyond its core European base, the exchange is seeding expansion in Japan and the US, indicating that rising global demand for energy risk management is broadening its addressable market.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership is capitalizing on favourable conditions by extending the product range and geographic footprint, reflecting a growth-oriented posture. Operational momentum appears healthy, though the narrative is drawn from a single brief market update. Insight into specific strategic trade-offs, competitive dynamics, or capital allocation choices remains limited, making it difficult to assess the depth of execution or long-term differentiation.",
